                                                        VELOCITY





Notes:

This sound represents a cathedral organ that can be used for heavy organ
solos in electronic rock styles, as well as some liturgical applications.
The light touch lets the velocity control the upper "stops" of the organ,
represented by upper footages. Playing with a more forced touch ( faster
velocity ) will bring in massive lower footages and octaves that will
be as powerful as a giant pipe organ. 

Treatment of this sound can be important. A solid reverb and a bit of
digital delay will enhance the sound of the organ, much like a large
room and natural delay adds to the perceived sound of the real instrument.














